          human: "Slovenian Tarok is the most popular parlour game in Slovenia, a point trick-taking game with bidding closely related to Austrian Tarock. 54 cards: 8 per suit (Clubs, Spades, Hearts, Diamonds) plus 22 trumps (taroks). Highest trump Å kis, then Mond (XXI), lowest trump (I). Black suits K-Q-Knight-J-10-9-8-7; red K-Q-Knight-J-1-2-3-4. Kings, Å kis, Mond, lowest trump 5 pts each; Queens 4, Knights 3, Jacks 2, others 1. Four players; dealer gives 12 cards each in two batches of 6 (counter-clockwise), 6 in talon. Bidding from Three up to Valat Without. With three/two/one declarer calls a King for secret partner. Declarer's side wins by taking more than half the card points.",
